course: dictionary
lesson: 3635
title: Fingertip and at your fingertips
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A fingertip is the very end of a finger. Your fingertips are where your fingerprints are, and they are the tips you use to touch, feel and pick things up.
explain: The phrase «information at your fingertips» means easy to reach and ready for you to use. The clue is «information»: it is something you can find or use quickly, just by reaching out.
explain: In «Sam wins by a fingertip», the words before it help you. Dev beats Sam by half a second every gala, so a win by a fingertip must be a tiny amount. Try your meaning in the sentence: «He wins by a very small amount» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A fingertip is the very end of a finger.
fact: «Fingertips» are packed with touch sensors, so they feel things very well.
fact: Fingertips can feel two points just 2 to 3 millimetres apart, but the back of your hand cannot feel them that close.
fact: «At your fingertips» means easy to reach or ready to use.
fact: Good hand washing cleans the fingertips, and so do the palms, the backs, the thumbs and the wrists.
exercise: «Sam wins by a fingertip» at the county gala. What does that mean? | By a long way, with lots of space to spare | *By a very small amount | By walking to the finish line | Without any swimming at all
exercise: Dad says the recipe is «information at your fingertips». What does that mean? | Written on the skin of your hands | *Easy to reach and ready to use | Lost somewhere in the kitchen | Hard to find and far away
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that names the very end of a finger: «Fingertips are packed with touch sensors.» | touch | packed | *fingertips | sensors
test: Why are fingertips good for reading Braille? | *They are very sensitive to touch, so they can feel tiny raised dots | They are the longest part of the hand | They can see the dots through the skin | They are always warm and wet
test: Which is the safest way to keep your fingertips safe? | Put your fingertips in a car door to hold it steady | Hold scissors by the blades | Test a blender with your fingertips while it is running | *Keep them away from car doors, scissors and blender blades
exam: The thumb can touch every «fingertip», which gives a strong, careful grip. What does fingertip mean here? | The bone in the wrist | *The very end of a finger | The back of the hand | The middle of the palm
